- genome/io.mjs, judge.mjs, lane.mjs, health.mjs and tombstone.mjs are the estate genome's hook template
  (sjgant80-hub/estate-genome), MIT, copyright Simon Gant, byte for byte.
- The problems are made by code (The Climb's generator, vendored). No dataset is used, and nothing in them describes a
  real person or company.
- vendor/fonts/ holds Fraunces, Hanken Grotesk and JetBrains Mono (variable, latin), each under the SIL Open Font
  Licence 1.1; each folder carries its licence. They are served from this page so that no font host is called.
- The model is not part of this repository. A round is run on Llama 3.2 1B Instruct (Meta, Llama 3.2 Community
  Licence), fetched by whoever runs it, with PyTorch, Hugging Face Transformers and PEFT (each under its own open
  licence). The records in data/ hold that model's replies to problems made by this repository's code.
- The adapters a round trains are not part of this repository either. Each is recorded by its SHA-256 in the round's
  verdict, with the training file and the settings that made it.
